        <body>
            <div xml:id="d622">

                <pb facs="1042" n="946" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg946"/>

                <head>No. 620.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">General Sickles to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation in Spain</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-11-17"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 17, 1873</date>.
                        (Received December 11.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 842.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to forward herewith a copy
                    and translation of a note received yesterday from Mr. Carvajal, under elate of
                    15th instant, assuring rne that the necessary orders have been sent to Cuba to
                    permit our consul to have access to the American citizens made prisoners on the
                    Virginius, and to assure to them the guarantees of the treaty of 1795, as
                    requested in my note of the 11th instant, of which a copy accompanied my No.
                    815. I am, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer><signed>D. E. SICKLES.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d622-a1.xml" xpointer="d622-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
